#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079282} :activity/id #uuid "5cd5b7c4-6c3f-5140-8338-e68375ee1c35" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050153 :topic/id #uuid "3210c88b-5df2-5409-97cd-3a2eb2370ffd" :topic/math-academy-id 665} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079282 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079720 :tutorial/content "Let's think about how to graph the solutions to the following two-variable inequality:\n\n$$\ny \\gt x\n$$\n\nSince this is a two-variable inequality, we must represent its solutions in the $xy$-plane.\n\nWe start by replacing the inequality symbol $(>)$ with an equals sign $(=)$ and plot the resulting line. In this case, we get the line $y=x$.\n\n![](images/34/3497eb8d3f071794cd899c5c62a88500fbcf7b69a34d58171866a078a185bfc9.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"*greater than*\" $(>)$ inequality. Therefore, we draw a *dashed* line to denote that points on the line are *not* solutions to our inequality.\n\nNow, since we're solving $y > x$, we need to shade all points whose $y$-value is *greater than* its $x$-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *above* our dashed line. So, let's shade these in.\n\n![](images/74/74fef6fbfabb750d09bba12b30f06bc9fd625ef824bdb3388bc66fe03a02c48c.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality $y > x$." :tutorial/id #uuid "ce943551-fa59-5976-8896-2c757f4b230a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8721 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "13f02de4-12fb-5e10-8f77-15e3768daca5" :step/math-academy-id 140701 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079283}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079283 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079721 :tutorial/content "When solving two-variable inequalities, it's often helpful to test to ensure we've shaded the correct region.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's go back to the following inequality:\n\n$$\ny > x\n$$\n\nThe solution to this inequality is indicated by the shaded region below.\n\n![](images/2c/2ceb4ad142fc943e9c5a95c43ba4e3a309669f09d383540fdfcb42f8cb48bf7c.png)\n\nTo check that we've shaded the correct region, we pick a point inside the shaded region and verify that it satisfies the original inequality. Let's pick the point $(0,1)$.\n\n![](images/29/29fc8bba0c205e7aa782fed0bb3cf348d4acc92b806eef60997917ade05905d5.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates $(0,1)$ into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}y & > x \\\\ 1 & > 0✓\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region." :tutorial/id #uuid "a4437a9f-4fe6-5dcf-a771-61bba9e944f1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8722 :tutorial/title "Testing the Solution"} :step/id #uuid "32db02a0-6340-58c0-9169-33c79dd56e21" :step/math-academy-id 140702 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079284}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079284 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078417 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078173 :question/id #uuid "7d1608fe-29b3-57de-9f32-b7c574b582c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-14035"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ad11090-d67b-5a5b-aaa7-2d9a5841b255" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049716} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050361} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050519}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078733} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079153}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution to a “Strictly Greater Than” Inequality"} :step/id #uuid "e65855e8-ad54-55a1-bb5a-f11caf0d33ee" :step/math-academy-id 140703 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079285}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079285 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079722 :tutorial/content "Let's now think about how to graph the solutions to the inequality\n\n$$\ny \\lt x\n$$\n\nAs before, we start by replacing the inequality symbol $(\\lt)$ with an equals sign $(=)$ and plot the resulting line $y=x$.\n\n![](images/72/72b217c75c8ec84681212a8ab48614fb777e05e7022ca338897d16763070c816.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"*less than*\" $(\\lt)$ inequality. Therefore, we draw a *dashed* line.\n\nNow, since we're solving $y \\lt x$, we need to shade all points whose $y$-value is *smaller than* its $x$-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *below* our dashed line.\n\n![](images/f7/f7259181cf578ae89840d42c752b9f36f84862a95dd3b03bc6e5b1aba7870e93.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality $y \\lt x$.\n\nTo check that we've shaded the correct region, we pick a point inside the shaded region and check that it satisfies the original inequality. Let's pick the point $(1,0)$.\n\n![](images/e3/e33d6402bfcbc4fad89775c451a0048f09aee83753b790ce9c98e465b3f374e1.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates $(1,0)$ into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}y & < x \\\\ 0 & < 1✓\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region." :tutorial/id #uuid "760096fa-2690-595f-b535-65cec94088a0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8731 :tutorial/title "Solving \"Strictly Less Than\" Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "3a3f7a76-f54b-5f7d-a7d3-11dc5d22fc4b" :step/math-academy-id 140706 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079286}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079286 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078418 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078174 :question/id #uuid "2fb1ec62-4417-5e4a-9fe1-23d667875e34" :question/math-academy-id "e-14046"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e4cee6-c73b-5894-b3f9-531f4cd41c66" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078717} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079141}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution to a “Strictly Less Than” Inequality"} :step/id #uuid "b463d728-7e47-511e-bed3-fc9201ebe3ef" :step/math-academy-id 140707 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079287}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079287 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078419 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078175 :question/id #uuid "df46228d-4744-5b2b-9886-8b6010f02a95" :question/math-academy-id "e-14059"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd738be-308a-54b8-aa4c-7acd6d60b691" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078773} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078784} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233750} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235492}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inequality Corresponding to a Given Graph"} :step/id #uuid "f0a9fe4e-160d-50d3-98a4-d6661bcfd764" :step/math-academy-id 140710}] :activity/title "Graphing Strict Two-Variable Linear Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186078681}]}
